From ecb5c1adccbd2711bfd0715062abe15ebdc4b6c6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pdale-boop <237306950+pdale-boop@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 19:13:03 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Aurora: a texture pack's optional/ folders load and drop
 while running, and the decode cache follows them

An optional/ folder can be loaded or dropped while running
(dol_aurora_set_texture_pack_optional), so a look that brings one can be
turned off and on in a session; the start's DOL_AURORA_TEXTURE_PACK_OPTIONAL
goes through the same call. Every change to the registered replacements bumps
a generation, and gxcore's decode cache (keyed by the guest's bytes, holding
the replacement or the decode it stood for) is cleared when it changes:
before, a texture seen once kept its first lookup, so HD's sky clouds stayed
after their folder went and, once dropped, did not come back. A background
decode carries its entry's id and is used only for that entry.
